---
title: Tytonidae
---
# Tytonidae

Tytonidae is the family of barn owls, nocturnal predators with a heart-shaped
facial disc and a serrated comb on the middle claw. They forage in near-total
darkness, and take prey located by hearing rather than by sight: the two ear
openings sit at different heights, so a sound reaches one a fraction before the
other and the difference resolves into an elevation. Some twenty species are
recognised, of which the [[barn-owl]] is much the most widespread.
